ory of that song how came about yeah I  mean you know it's it's like with any of  my songs you know it always comes a  little bit sometimes from my own  experience but this was something I was  talking with a friend of mine about we  were both kind of fresh out of  relationships and we both were the  people that had broken them off and you  know and we were just kind of talking  about the fact that it kind of doesn't  matter like what happened in the  relationship or what the reasons were  why you broke up if you're the one that  leaves you kind of always the bad guy in  to everybody else you know and and it's  almost like it's assumed that it was  just easier for you somehow because you  made the decision which is which is not  always the case it's it's a different  kind of hurt and it's a different kind  of pain and it's a different perspective  and so I just wanted to write something  that spoke to that perspective of a  breakup female artists are doing it's so  big in country right now you must be  getting a lot of messages on social  media a lot of people talking to you  like young girls that want to come up  and do it you're doing what's it like  talking to them it's amazing I mean when  I have I mean just in general when I  have fans reach out to me whether  they're trying to be in music or they're  doing that themselves or not you know  and I just have somebody reach out and  say this song changed my life or it's it  is everything right now and I felt like  you just reached inside of my brain and  took out what I was thinking and I  relate to it but when I have you know  young female artists that that look up  to me and you know want to do what I'm  doing I mean it's it's it's a really  cool feeling because I was that little  girl once you know and so when I get to  see that it's a really cool full circle  moment and it's also a good reminder for  me sometimes because I'm very hard on  myself you know it's a good reminder  that I'm further ahead than I think